title Mycelium Chorus r3 — a quorum's agreed position survives a checkpoint
prompt baton prin recur — read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think r1 made a Chorus (a quorum of independent Vouchers) believed only when a threshold of distinct nodes agree; r2 let the whole quorum travel as bytes. Yet a ledger a family runs for years does not carry its past unbroken — the Knot ties off a committed prefix into a sealed supply, and the Lapse continues its deadline clock across the seal by carrying the epoch base. r3 (mirroring voucher_knot / statement_knot) reads a whole quorum over a ledger resolved across an epoch cut.
think Studied voucher_knot.rye: its check_position_across verifies one voucher's signature offline then confirms the vouched triple equals the continued ledger's reading (r1's check_against needs the whole Dag, which a checkpointing party no longer holds). Lifted that to the quorum: chorus_knot.check_position_across(c, ledger, threshold) re-runs r1's whole quorum law (every member verifies, all agree, distinct signers, count met) then confirms the one agreed triple against the Knot-continued reading. Reused voucher_knot's Scene/seat/whole_dag/prefix_dag/continue_across helpers verbatim (genesis credits Alice 100, Alice pledges 100 to Bob, Alice posts; prefix = genesis+pledge, suffix = post).
obs GREEN on the first build and run across four movements: the crux (deadline 2 lapses across the cut — Alice's coins home, balance 100/reserved 0/received 100; a three-node quorum gathered against the whole Cord is believed at threshold 3, checks against the whole Dag, and its agreed position reads true through the Knot-continued ledger where lapsed_seen()==1; Bob's quorum too), the seam (deadline 5 honored in the suffix — Bob credited across the base reads his whole 100 inflow, never a restart, the quorum true to the pruned history; Alice's reserved returned), the whole-history fingerprint (the whole three-block order-head differs from the prefix-only head in the claim AND in every member — asserted per member — so no node can silently name a shorter order; check_against whole passes, check_against prefix fails), and tamper (a forged member breaks the quorum → check_position_across false; a thin threshold of 4 → false; a Knot corrupted after sealing → KnotCorrupt before any position is read).
obs Additive: composes chorus + voucher + statement + lapse_knot + lapse + cord + fold + kumara public API only, editing none (the Chorus r1 and the Lapse-Knot re-run GREEN at the door). Witness tools/mycelium_chorus_knot_witness.rish GREEN, TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0. Demo keeper seeds — no key/funds/network/custody; a mesh reads its own attestations across its own sealed checkpoint.
loom witness=mycelium_chorus_knot_witness movements=4 threshold=3 first_build=green
file mycelium/chorus_knot.rye r3 — check_position_across (re-run the quorum law, then confirm the agreed triple against a Knot-continued ledger), the whole-history order-head seam
file tools/mycelium_chorus_knot_witness.rish the r3 witness — survives-checkpoint + received-accumulates + whole-history-head + tamper assertions, the Chorus and Lapse-Knot re-run at the door
recommend keep-going Chorus r4 (true to the bytes — a real on-disk Cord fixture, the agreed triple app == awk, the distinct-node count and each member's recomputed order-head matching the signed ones), then the arc closes and a remember fold cards it. A served chorus · per-account mint authority · breach renames (cairn-first) · deep debride · seed force-push stay the maintainer's hand.
